 `CORE_BUILD_P2_HOST` includes the historical artifact-only host used by regression
 tests. `build/graph/core/kaos_host` is the complete current graph host.
 For sanitizer checks, configure a separate build with `-DCORE_SANITIZE=ON`.
+
+The current host uses distinct management and application UDP ports. `GraphRun`
+allocates both and supplies the new command line automatically; rebuild the host
+and update the simulator together. Direct launch syntax is
+`kaos_host management_port application_port authority_port device_id authority_id`
+followed by `peer_id:management_port:application_port` for every remote device.
+Readiness is `LISTENING management_port application_port`. O and the collector
+use management-only routes. The historical P2 artifact-only fixture is unchanged.
+
+`run.network.addresses[device]["management"]` and `["application"]` expose the
+relay addresses. Both classes share the directed-link loss/delay/duplication
+policy and random stream, and all links/classes share one bounded pending-copy
+queue. Separate ports do not create independent impairment or Wi-Fi priorities.
+The host serves bounded application batches, management every round, and paced
+artifact requests; see the [scheduler and verification](../kaos_core/guide/verification.md#two-port-transport-scheduling).
 
